{"tool_name":"screadcounts","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"screadcounts","home":"https://github.com/HorvathLab/NGS/tree/master/SCReadCounts","summary":"Estimation of cell-level SNVs from scRNA-seq data.\n\nSCReadCounts is a computational tool for a cell-level assessment of the read counts bearing a particular nucleotide at genomic positions of interest from single cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data.\n\nSCReadCounts is available as a self-contained binary package for 64-bit Linux systems, as Python source, and MacOS (Darwin). The self-contained binary package is appropriate for most Linux and MacOS users. The pythonic version requires pysam, numpy and scipy along with other packages (See the install instructions for more details).","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:57:28Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-13T16:13:05Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:screadcounts","credit":[{"email":"horvatha@gwu.edu","name":"Anelia Horvath","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Haplotype mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0487"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"SCReadCounts","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.11.23.394569"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SCReadCounts","home":"https://bio.tools/screadcounts","summary":"Estimation of cell-level SNVs from scRNA-seq data.\n\nSCReadCounts is a computational tool for a cell-level assessment of the read counts bearing a particular nucleotide at genomic positions of interest from single cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data.\n\nSCReadCounts is available as a self-contained binary pack